new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f8fc990
--- /dev/null
+++ b/SOLUTION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+# SOLUTION
+
+Two bugs in `lrucache/cache.py`:
+
+1. **`get` did not refresh recency.** It returned the value without moving the
+   key to the end of the `OrderedDict`, so a recently-read entry was still
+   treated as least-recently-used and could be wrongly evicted. Fixed by
+   calling `self._data.move_to_end(key)` on a successful `get`.
+
+2. **`put` evicted an entry even when updating an existing key.** The
+   capacity check ran unconditionally, so re-putting a key that was already
+   present evicted the oldest entry even though the cache size was not
+   growing. Fixed by only popping when `key not in self._data`.
